From: kodi-ps4 dev <dev@kodi-ps4.local>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 19:42:03 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 11/12] ps4: keep SQLite temporary b-trees in memory

The reduced 128-page cache spills the repository catalog ORDER BY to a temporary file; Orbis has no usable temporary path, and SQLite fails with SQLITE_IOERR_GETTEMPPATH on an empty filename. Use PRAGMA temp_store=MEMORY on Orbis so the sorter stays in the flexible heap.
---
 xbmc/dbwrappers/sqlitedataset.cpp | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/xbmc/dbwrappers/sqlitedataset.cpp b/xbmc/dbwrappers/sqlitedataset.cpp
index 53b6232a70..8340d73ce0 100644
--- a/xbmc/dbwrappers/sqlitedataset.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/dbwrappers/sqlitedataset.cpp
@@ -435,8 +435,11 @@ int SqliteDatabase::postconnect()
     throw DbErrors("Cannot execute postconnect actions: no active connection...");
 
 #if defined(__ORBIS__)
+  // The catalog query sorts more rows than the reduced page cache can hold.
+  // Keep the temporary b-tree in memory: Orbis has no usable temp path.
   static const char* sqlcmd{
-      "PRAGMA cache_size=128; PRAGMA synchronous='NORMAL'; PRAGMA count_changes='OFF';"};
+      "PRAGMA cache_size=128; PRAGMA temp_store=MEMORY; PRAGMA synchronous='NORMAL'; "
+      "PRAGMA count_changes='OFF';"};
 #else
   static const char* sqlcmd{
       "PRAGMA cache_size=4096; PRAGMA synchronous='NORMAL'; PRAGMA count_changes='OFF';"};
